{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory handled the immediate neonatal post-discharge risk well: it repeatedly checked current stability, set urgent ED thresholds, used the discharge information, arranged follow-up, and created a family night-shift plan. However, the home observation/checklist never clearly converted urine output/diaper tracking into an ongoing executable item and the discharge follow-up plan omitted the required vaccine/screening verification, which are minor responsibility-chain omissions. Under the frozen rubric, any minor responsibility-chain error caps the grade at 2 despite several high-order strengths.",
